.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/eslint-plugin-react-refresh Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "eslint-plugin-react-refresh [![npm](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/eslint-plugin-react-refresh)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/eslint-plugin-react-refresh)"
.PP
Validate that your components can safely be updated with Fast Refresh\&.
.SH "Explainer"
.PP
"Fast Refresh", also known as "hot reloading", is a feature in many modern bundlers\&. If you update some React component(s) on disk, then the bundler will know to update only the impacted parts of your page -- without a full page reload\&.

.PP
\fReslint-plugin-react-refresh\fP enforces that your components are structured in a way that integrations such as \fRreact-refresh\fP expect\&.
.SS "Limitations"
⚠️ To avoid false positives, by default this plugin is only applied on \fRtsx\fP & \fRjsx\fP files\&. See \fBOptions\fP to run on JS files\&. ⚠️

.PP
The plugin relies on naming conventions (i\&.e\&. use PascalCase for components, camelCase for util functions)\&. This is why there are some limitations:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRexport *\fP are not supported and will be reported as an error
.IP "\(bu" 2
Anonymous function are not supported (i\&.e \fRexport default function() {}\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Class components are not supported
.IP "\(bu" 2
All-uppercase function export is considered an error when not using direct named export (ex \fRconst CMS = () => <></>; export { CMS }\fP)
.PP
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm i \-D eslint\-plugin\-react\-refresh
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
This plugin provides a single rule, \fRreact-refresh/only-export-components\fP\&. There are multiple ways to enable it\&.
.SS "Recommended config"
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";
import reactRefresh from "eslint\-plugin\-react\-refresh";

export default defineConfig(
  /* Main config */
  reactRefresh\&.configs\&.recommended,
);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Vite config"
This enables the \fRallowConstantExport\fP option which is supported by Vite React plugins\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";
import reactRefresh from "eslint\-plugin\-react\-refresh";

export default defineConfig(
  /* Main config */
  reactRefresh\&.configs\&.vite,
);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Next config (v0\&.4\&.21)"
This allows exports like \fRfetchCache\fP and \fRrevalidate\fP which are used in Page or Layout components and don't trigger a full page reload\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";
import reactRefresh from "eslint\-plugin\-react\-refresh";

export default defineConfig(
  /* Main config */
  reactRefresh\&.configs\&.next,
);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Without config"
.PP
.nf
import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";
import reactRefresh from "eslint\-plugin\-react\-refresh";

export default defineConfig({
  // in main config for TSX/JSX source files
  plugins: {
    "react\-refresh": reactRefresh,
  },
  rules: {
    "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": "error",
  },
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "Legacy config"
.PP
.nf
{
  "plugins": ["react\-refresh"],
  "rules": {
    "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": "error",
  },
}
.fi
.PP
.SH "Examples"
.PP
These examples are from enabling \fRreact-refresh/only-exports-components\fP\&.
.SS "Fail"
.PP
.nf
export const foo = () => {};
export const Bar = () => <></>;
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
export default function () {}
export default compose()(MainComponent)
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
export * from "\&./foo";
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const Tab = () => {};
export const tabs = [<Tab />, <Tab />];
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const App = () => {};
createRoot(document\&.getElementById("root"))\&.render(<App />);
.fi
.PP
.SS "Pass"
.PP
.nf
export default function Foo() {
  return <></>;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const foo = () => {};
export const Bar = () => <></>;
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
import { App } from "\&./App";
createRoot(document\&.getElementById("root"))\&.render(<App />);
.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
These options are all present on \fRreact-refresh/only-exports-components\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
interface Options {
  allowExportNames?: string[];
  allowConstantExport?: boolean;
  customHOCs?: string[];
  checkJS?: boolean;
}

const defaultOptions: Options = {
  allowExportNames: [],
  allowConstantExport: false,
  customHOCs: [],
  checkJS: false,
};
.fi
.PP
.SS "allowExportNames (v0\&.4\&.4)"
.RS 4
Default: \fR[]\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
If you use a framework that handles HMR of some specific exports, you can use this option to avoid warning for them\&.

.PP
Example for \fRRemix\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": [
    "error",
    { "allowExportNames": ["meta", "links", "headers", "loader", "action"] }
  ]
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "allowConstantExport (v0\&.4\&.0)"
.RS 4
Default: \fRfalse\fP (\fRtrue\fP in \fRvite\fP config) 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Don't warn when a constant (string, number, boolean, templateLiteral) is exported aside one or more components\&.

.PP
This should be enabled if the fast refresh implementation correctly handles this case (HMR when the constant doesn't change, propagate update to importers when the constant changes\&.)\&. Vite supports it, PR welcome if you notice other integrations works well\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": [
    "error",
    { "allowConstantExport": true }
  ]
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Enabling this option allows code such as the following:

.PP
.PP
.nf
export const CONSTANT = 3;
export const Foo = () => <></>;
.fi
.PP
.SS "checkJS (v0\&.3\&.3)"
.RS 4
Default: \fRfalse\fP 
.RE
.PP

.PP
If you're using JSX inside \fR\&.js\fP files (which I don't recommend because it forces you to configure every tool you use to switch the parser), you can still use the plugin by enabling this option\&. To reduce the number of false positive, only files importing \fRreact\fP are checked\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": ["error", { "checkJS": true }]
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "customHOCs (v0\&.4\&.15)"
If you're exporting a component wrapped in a custom HOC, you can use this option to avoid false positives\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  "react\-refresh/only\-export\-components": [
    "error",
    { "customHOCs": ["observer", "withAuth"] }
  ]
}
.fi
.PP
 
